<article class="env-lemma" id="0EBP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EBP">Lemma <span data-tag="0EBP">31.30.4</span>.</a> Assumptions and notation as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0EBN" data-tag="0EBN">31.30.3</a>. If $s$ is nonzero, then every irreducible component of $X \setminus U$ has codimension $1$ in $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\xi \in X$ be a generic point of an irreducible component $Z$ of $X \setminus U$. After replacing $X$ by an open neighbourhood of $\xi $ we may assume that $Z = X \setminus U$ is irreducible. Since $s : \mathcal{O}_ U \to \mathcal{F}|_ U$ is an isomorphism, if the codimension of $Z$ in $X$ is $\geq 2$, then $s : \mathcal{O}_ X \to \mathcal{F}$ is an isomorphism by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EBJ" data-tag="0EBJ">31.13.12</a> and Serre's criterion Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0345" data-tag="0345">28.12.5</a>. This would mean that $Z = \emptyset $, a contradiction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>